    "text": "Source port number: 16 bits long port number used by the process running on the source host. Destination port number: 16 bits long port number used by the process running on the destination host. Length: This ts a 16-bit field that defines the total length of the user datagram, header plus data. The 16 bits can define a total length of 0 to 65,535 bytes. Length field in a UDP user datagram is not necessary as user datagram 1s encapsulated in IP datagram. A field in IP datagram defines total length and another field defines header length.",
